.nf
YASMV manual                                           read-trace

.ti 0
SYNOPSIS

.in 3
read-trace '<filepath>'

.ti 0
DESCRIPTION

.fi
.in 3
Reads a trace from the given filename. A .json file must contain one trace v1
object. Its model identity, types, values, initialization, invariants,
transitions, and generating query are validated before it is registered and
selected. The matching model and input bindings must already be loaded.

Other extensions use the legacy plain-text reader; YAML is unsupported.
See docs/QUERY_AND_TRACE_CONTRACTS.md for the JSON format and migration notes.

NOTICE: due to a limitation of the parser, file paths must ALWAYS be specified
enclosed in either single or double quotes. Paths not enclosed in quotes will
*not* be correctly parsed.


.ti 0
EXAMPLES

.nf
>> read-trace 'examples/ferryman/ferryman.json'


